What is the output of the following Java program demonstrating the 'classes win' rule?
```java
interface Greeter {
    default void sayHello() { System.out.print("Interface "); }
}
abstract class BaseGreeter {
    public void sayHello() { System.out.print("Class "); }
}
class FriendlyGreeter extends BaseGreeter implements Greeter {}
public class GreeterApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Greeter g = new FriendlyGreeter();
        g.sayHello();
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program comparing static method inheritance across classes and interfaces?
